", "id": 8816838, "raw_content": "On September 2, 2026, U.S. military forces, operating under U.S. Southern Command (SOUTHCOM) and in coordination with Ecuador, intercepted and sank a vessel in the Eastern Pacific that intelligence confirmed was supporting the Los Choneros narco-terrorist organization.  \r\n\r\nMarines and sailors from the USS San Antonio boarded, searched, and cleared the vessel without incident before removing multiple individuals who were transferred to Ecuadorian authorities. \r\nThe vessel, described as a floating refueling station, was targeted to cut off a critical node in illicit at-sea drug trafficking logistics. ", "author": "Bullet3250", "created": 1788525891175, "profile_picture": "", "community": "TheDonald", "ad_tier": 2, "last_comment_author": "", "is_video": false, "video_link": "", "is_new_user": false, "domain": "", "is_crosspost": false, "preview": "", "removal_source": "", "link": "", "author_flair_class": "", "is_removed": false, "media": {"resized_resolutions": [], "blurhash": "", "full_resolution": []}, "title": "US Military Says It Sank Los Choneros Cartel Support Vessel in Pacific", "last_comment_created": 1788525891174, "content": "<p>On September 2, 2026, U.S. military forces, operating under U.S. Southern Command (SOUTHCOM) and in coordination with Ecuador, intercepted and sank a vessel in the Eastern Pacific that intelligence confirmed was supporting the Los Choneros narco-terrorist organization.</p>\n<p>Marines and sailors from the USS San Antonio boarded, searched, and cleared the vessel without incident before removing multiple individuals who were transferred to Ecuadorian authorities.\nThe vessel, described as a floating refueling station, was targeted to cut off a critical node in illicit at-sea drug trafficking logistics.</p>\n", "score_down": 0, "author_flair_text": "", "pro_tier": 0, "is_stickied": false, "is_nsfw": false, "is_deleted": false, "is_image": false, "comments": 0, "score_up": 23, "is_edited": false,